.SH NATIVE SYSTEM BOOT SELECTION
For an initialized native-v2 image, system select --deployment ID
--expected-selected ID changes the next boot only.
Use --dry-run to preview or -y to apply.  system rollback
--expected-selected ID selects the validated previous deployment.
Both require an administrator, preserve exact Base and Kernel, retain old
content and do not reboot or activate services live.
.PP
System status distinguishes installed artifacts, admitted boot deployments,
the selected next boot and explicit running evidence.  Unknown running identity
is not inferred from a generation label or uname.  Native-v2 selection refuses
content-only or diagnostic slots and refuses stale expected selection.
.PP
Initial image assembly and constructor admission use the manager API.
Automatic installed System staging from an active v2 baseline and boot wish
integration remain incomplete; v1 writers cannot change a v2 boot authority.
